WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.791
Spell-checkers, search boxes and password rules all process text one character at a time. Let’s learn how.

2
00:00:09.391 --> 00:00:19.322
Text is a string of characters, each with a position. letter (1) of [apple] is a; length of [apple] is 5.

3
00:00:19.922 --> 00:00:27.243
Same pattern as lists: i from 1 to the length, read letter i each time.

4
00:00:27.843 --> 00:00:32.991
Start with an empty string and join letters onto it.

5
00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:37.704
Joining each letter to the FRONT reverses the word.

6
00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:43.017
A palindrome reads the same backwards: level, racecar, noon.

7
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:47.730
Reverse the word and compare it with the original.

8
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:56.957
In Python, a for loop can walk through the characters of a string, just like our Scratch loop.

9
00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:01.400
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

10
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:06.548
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
